  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Regarding the new Twitch Guidelines: https://t.co/g4PbA9pOf9\nI thought of a possibility to make it safer for streamers (of course if Avatar creators go with it)\nso my Idea was to make an option in the VRCSDK when uploading an Avatar just like the privat or puplic option.\nfor example add 3 options\n-Streamsafe\n-unsure\n-not Safe\n-and a fourth option, that does nothing and will be only applied to all avatars that are precreated and every avatar that has still that fourth option on a certain date will be changed to \"not Safe\" so avatar creators are needed to change there option in \"manage content\" to the appropiate setting.\n\nbecause I know alot of people don´t know if their avatar would be safe and I don´t believe anyone would like to get rid of their hard work on an avatar that is now against the TwitchToS\nI think that would be for now the safest option.\nalso for making sure everyone understands what is safe or not maybe add a Graphic that show what parts on either a female or male avatar has to be covered by clothing from front and back on either upload next to it where you choose your option or a specified link to an explanation\nand now to the safety setting ingame:\nadd an option in the safety settings menu where you can choose if u want to see all avatars or hide \"not safe\" avatars or even hide \"unsure\" avatars (regardless of other safety settings or if a person is set to \"show avatar\")\nI myself fall in the category of being an avatar creator and I love every single avatar I have and really don´t want to bring any streamer into problems",
